 near Kanchipuram in south-eastern India, during the Second Anglo-Mysore War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-malplaquet"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-malplaquet.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Malplaquet</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 11 September 1709</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Malplaquet was fought on 11 September 1709 near Mons, in Hainaut, during the War of the Spanish Succession.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ascalon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-ascalon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Ascalon</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 12 August 1099</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Ascalon was fought on 12 August 1099 near Ascalon on the coast of southern Palestine, soon after the capture of Jerusalem in the First Crusade.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-durbe"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-durbe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Durbe</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 13 July 1260</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Durbe was fought on 13 July 1260 near Durbe in present-day western Latvia, where Samogitian forces routed the combined army of the Livonian Order and the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-winwaed"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-winwaed.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Winwaed</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 15 November 655</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Winwaed was fought on 15 November 655, probably near Leeds, when Oswiu of Northumbria defeated and killed the pagan king Penda of Merc